largely|Mostly permits non-volunteer exceptions, not total authorship. Vietnamese chủ yếu preserves degree; no restriction to passive past forms is inferred.
reflection|Image and deliberation are distinct ordinals. Bridge water scene versus plan revision match noun boundaries; Vietnamese does not confuse thought with visible reflection.
tax|Required payment and imposing it have separate POS. Receipt and fictional authority examples avoid actual rates/legal guidance; source rights are not inferred from a tax record.
whoever|PRONOUN Oxford evidence used for any qualifying person; conflicting NOUN evidence is not promoted. First arrival and seat permission preserved; clause-function note is grammatical, not a new canonical entity.
any|Question amount, unrestricted choice, stand-alone pronoun and comparative degree differ meaningfully. Free-choice det boundary has no specific ordinal claim; translations retain question polarity and negative easier comparison, not a forced duplicate Sense split.
